  "slides": [
    {
      "page_title": "Moving State Without Destroying",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "terraform state mv 'aws_instance.web[0]' \\",
            "  'aws_instance.web[\"a\"]'   # count->for_each",
            "terraform state mv -state-out=../o/terraform.tfstate \\",
            "  aws_instance.web aws_instance.web"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "moved Blocks Beat state mv"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "hcl",
          "lines": [
            "moved {",
            "  from = aws_instance.web",
            "  to   = aws_instance.api",
            "}"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "state mv",
                "lines": [
                  "imperative",
                  "one machine",
                  "not reviewable"
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "moved block",
                "lines": [
                  "declarative",
                  "travels in repo",
                  "runs for every operator"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Module consumers get the refactor for free",
            "Keep moved blocks one release cycle after the rename",
            "Delete once every consumer has applied"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Forgetting Without Deleting"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "hcl",
          "lines": [
            "removed {",
            "  from = aws_instance.legacy",
            "  lifecycle { destroy = false }",
            "}",
            "# declarative form of state rm"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`terraform state rm` forgets, never deletes",
            "Standard way to hand ownership to another state",
            "Note the ID first so you can import it back"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Danger of state rm",
          "items": [
            "The resource becomes an unmanaged orphan",
            "Nothing will ever clean it up",
            "It keeps billing you quietly"
          ],
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "terraform state replace-provider \\",
            "  registry.terraform.io/-/aws \\",
            "  registry.terraform.io/hashicorp/aws"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Proof of a Good Move",
          "text": "`state pull > pre-move.tfstate` first, then plan. A non-empty plan means the move was wrong — restore the backup, don't apply."
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Splitting a monolith: move out with `-state-out`",
            "Push both halves, verify plans are empty",
            "Delete the old code last — order matters"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Import: Adopting Existing Infrastructure",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What Import Does",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Binds a real object to a Terraform address",
            "Writes state only",
            "Never creates or modifies infrastructure"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "terraform import aws_instance.web i-0abc123",
            "# config block must already exist",
            "terraform import 'module.vpc.aws_subnet.public[0]' \\",
            "  subnet-abc123"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Import IDs Vary"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Resource",
            "Import ID"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`aws_instance`",
              "`i-0abc123`"
            ],
            [
              "`aws_s3_bucket`",
              "bucket name"
            ],
            [
              "`aws_iam_role`",
              "role name"
            ],
            [
              "sg rule",
              "composite string"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Check provider docs per resource, every time",
            "Importing into a missing address just errors",
            "The obvious ID is often not the right one"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Post-Import Loop"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "write config",
              "import",
              "plan",
              "edit config",
              "empty plan"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Empty Plan = Proof",
          "text": "Expect a diff on the first plan. Edit config until the plan is empty — that is the only proof config matches reality."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "import Blocks"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "hcl",
          "lines": [
            "import {",
            "  to = aws_instance.web",
            "  id = \"i-0abc123\"",
            "}",
            "# works with for_each: bulk adoption"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Reviewable in a PR, applied by `terraform apply`",
            "CLI import handles one resource per invocation",
            "One-shot: delete after apply or they go no-op",
            "Stale import blocks just make plans noisy"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "terraform plan -generate-config-out=gen.tf",
            "# writes candidate HCL for import blocks",
            "# a starting point, not finished code"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Import: Adopting Existing Infrastructure (cont.)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "No Dependencies Come Along",
          "items": [
            "Importing an EC2 instance imports only that",
            "Security group, subnet, EBS stay unmanaged",
            "Each needs its own import"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Terraformer and former2 do bulk brownfield adoption",
            "Generated HCL is verbose and needs refactoring",
            "Same object in two states = both configs fight"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "How do I trust an import?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "`terraform state show <address>` after importing",
            "Compare key attributes against the console",
            "Only then trust the empty plan",
            "Import is also the recovery tool after `state rm`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "State Holds Secrets",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "RDS master passwords land in the JSON",
            "So do generated private keys",
            "Any `sensitive` variable reaching an attribute",
            "All in plaintext, always"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Mitigations"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`encrypt = true` on S3, plus a KMS key",
            "Restrict bucket reads by IAM",
            "Reference a secret store instead of generating secrets",
            "OpenTofu adds client-side state encryption"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Backend-Level Only",
          "text": "Terraform relies on backend encryption: anyone who can read the object can read the secrets."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Recovery Ladder"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flowchart",
          "spec": {
            "title": "state lost",
            "rows": [
              [
                "n0"
              ],
              [
