        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Versioning makes recovery a one-command fix",
            "Rebuilding by hand-import is slow and error-prone",
            "Confirm `serial` and `lineage` before pushing back"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "cont": true
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Security, Disasters, Rules That Save You",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Mistakes That Cost Real Money"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Mistake",
            "Consequence"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "laptop local state",
              "no lock, dies with machine"
            ],
            [
              "destroy, wrong workspace",
              "prod gone"
            ],
            [
              "hand-edited JSON",
              "nonsense plans"
            ],
            [
              "`state rm` to hide a plan",
              "orphan still billing"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Mistake",
            "Consequence"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "two configs, one resource",
              "flip-flopping diff"
            ],
            [
              "one giant company state",
              "slow plans, total blast radius"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Guard destroys with `prevent_destroy` on stateful resources",
            "Require an approval step in CI",
            "Directory-per-environment beats workspace discipline"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Right-Sizing States"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Split by lifecycle and ownership",
            "Network, data, compute per service",
            "Each state small, fast, owned by one team"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "CI Checklist",
          "items": [
            "Plan on PR with `-detailed-exitcode`",
            "Apply saved plan files only",
            "`-lock-timeout` always set",
            "Credentials scoped per environment; bucket versioned"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "The Whole Model",
          "text": "State maps addresses to real IDs. The backend makes that map shared, durable and locked. Drift is the map diverging from the world."
        },
        {
